<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lembitu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1217">1217</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Lembitu of Lehola</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lembitu was an Estonian elder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagala">Sakala</a>, based at the hillfort of Lehola, who led resistance to the German crusaders in the early 13th century. He built alliances among the Estonian lands and sought help from Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a>. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-matthews-day">Battle of St Matthew's Day</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viljandi">Viljandi</a> in September 1217, and he is remembered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lembitu.jpg" alt="Lembitu" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vaido Otsar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suure-Jaani_Vabaduss%C3%B5ja_m%C3%A4lestussammas_2018_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
